Original commit body from 4446fe3af554016ae09bf042d1aa6eb1269ce3c1:

The per-PR gate announced `964 selected files` for PR #1107, whose committed
manifest listed 75, ran ~29,680 tests, and dragged three unrelated latent
defects through five CI rounds. 964 is not arbitrary: it is exactly
`find packages/*/tests tests \( -name 'test_*.py' -o -name
'BRANCHES_test_*.py' \) | wc -l` at that SHA -- smart-test's full-suite
fallback. The original filing ruled that out by counting 850 test files and
observing 964 > 850; the count was `test_*.py` only and missed the 116
`BRANCHES_test_*.py` the writer also takes.

Root cause: smart-test decides which repo it means from its OWN location
(`REPO_ROOT="$(cd "$(dirname "$0")/.." && pwd)"`, then `cd "$REPO_ROOT"`) and
writes the literal relative path `.ci/affected-tests.txt`. The caller's cwd
never enters the decision, so `/A/scripts/smart-test` run from inside repo `/B`
produces no manifest for `/B` and does not fail -- it rewrites `/A`'s committed
artifact. Ten `tests/test_autopr_*.py` modules drive the real `scripts/auto-pr`
from a fixture repo, and auto-pr regenerates the manifest before pushing.

In CI the steps share one workspace. `forge-arms` installs pytest and nothing
else and runs `tests/test_autopr_*.py`, so the regen took the "no stable
hypergumbo found" branch and wrote a full-suite manifest over the checked-out
one; the `pytest` step waits on build-grammars and read it much later. The case
self-healed when the offending test was made hermetic in 0f0f345415, which is
why nothing reproduced it afterwards.

Fixed at the writer: a cwd inside a DIFFERENT git repo is refused with exit 3,
naming both roots and both ways out. Scoped to the case shown to bite -- a cwd
in no git repo names no competing manifest and keeps today's behaviour.

Fixed at the reader too: the per-PR pytest step reads the blob committed at
HEAD, prints the header of the manifest it actually read (the step's only
selection output was a count, which is untraceable to a file), and discloses
any disagreement. It discloses rather than fails: measuring the committed
artifact is the safety property, and turning an unexplained rewrite into a red
PR is the recall-loss direction.

Verified against the original repro -- before: the real manifest's md5 changed
while the foreign repo got nothing; after: refusal printed, exit 3, md5
unchanged. 410 passed across the auto-pr/smart-test/CI slice, 1996 across the
full affected slice. The control arm in the CI gate is mutation-tested.

